{%- comment -%}
  PG R36S Ultra Story (2026-09-23): cloned from the R36S Pro page's story
  section for the R36S Ultra page, registered in
  templates/product.pg-ultra.json only. Renamed to the uls prefix; the price
  comparison and the buttons read the Ultra tiles (.pg-ul / data-ul); the
  accessory cards use the r36s-ultra-* add-ons; every hardware claim is the
  Ultra spec's (under the title, Built-in Wi-Fi and 4-Inch HD Screen replace
  the Pro's No WiFi Needed and 6-Hour Battery); the two photos are picked by
  alt; and the Judge.me photo strip and its "loved by" pill are removed,
  because this product's Judge.me reviews were imported for the Flip SP and
  must not show on this page. The notes below are the Pro page's history
  (2026-09-17 on), kept for reference.

  The selling sections, by request, modelled on the layout of a competitor's
  page but in our own words, colors and claims.

  THE PIECES, EACH SEATED BY THE SCRIPT AT THE BOTTOM:
    1. BENEFITS (.pg-uls-ben): four pain points answered, icon plus one line,
       directly under the title and stars. No paragraph, by request. The third
       is battery life (it was "Save Anywhere"; swapped by request, and saving
       is still covered in the chart).
       THE FOURTH IS "ADD YOUR OWN GAMES" (2026-09-17, by request: replace the
       30 day returns one "with something describing how you can put any games
       you want on the system", and say it in Under the hood and the chart
       too). It took the place of "30-Day Returns", which the guarantee bar
       and the info box under the bundles still say. Under the hood: it
       replaced "Pick Up Where You Left Off" (saving keeps its chart row). The
       chart has a row for it. The wording is "your own game files" throughout
       and names no game.
       THE NUMBER OF GAMES RIDES WITH THE FIRST ICON (2026-09-17). On a phone
       the icons show their bold labels only, so "Up to 40K" had dropped off
       the top of the page. It was first put back as a line of its own under
       the title, which is not what was meant ("undo that and put it with the
       icon"): the first label now reads "Up to 40K" on its own line over
       "Games Preloaded". White like the rest of the label; it was lavender
       for a few hours ("doesnt need to be in purple"). "Up to", because the
       Single Device carries 15,000+.
    2. BUYER PHOTOS (.pg-uls-shots): a swipeable strip of the photo reviews
       Judge.me holds for this product, under the rotating review card at the
       foot of the buy column. Headed "Buyer Reviews" by request. It is built
       from judgeme.review_widget_data and renders nothing when there are no
       photo reviews. NOTE (2026-09-17): the photos in that feed are served
       from ae-pic-a1.aliexpress-media.com, so these are imported supplier
       reviews, not reviews collected by this store. Raised with the owner.
       THE WHOLE CONSOLE LEADS (2026-09-17: "only show the good photos first,
       like showing the whole item"). The feed opened on a circuit board and an
       open battery bay. Every photo was looked at: the four that show the
       whole console front on come first (lead_keys, in that order), the open
       back and circuit board shots go to the end, and last of all the two
       whose screens show a recognisable game (last_keys). A photo is named by
       the file id in its URL and placed with flex order, so nothing is
       removed and a new photo review lands in the middle until it is sorted.
       SUPERSEDED 2026-09-22: the strip now shows every photo of every review
       but only from an allow list of the sharp ones (hq_keys, in display
       order), and swiping it never reaches an end. See the notes at hq_keys and at
       loopRail() in the script.
    3. THE STORY (#pg-uls): nostalgia headline, the used-handheld price
       comparison, four feature blocks, the comparison chart and a button back
       up to the bundles. Moved in above the bottom review grid.

  EVERY CLAIM IS ONE THE PRODUCT PAGE ALREADY MAKES (description / specs). On
  the Ultra page that is the Ultra spec only (2026-09-23): 15,000+ games on
  64GB and 40K on 128GB, 20+ systems, RK3326 1.5GHz + 1GB RAM, 4 inch 720x720
  IPS fully laminated, built-in 2.4G Wi-Fi, 3000mAh for about 5 hours. The
  spec names no memory card slot, so none is mentioned. The starting price
  is printed from product.price_min, so it follows the admin.
  The used-handheld figure is a SETTING, because it is a market price and it
  moves: on 2026-09-17 PriceCharting listed a loose Game Boy Advance SP
  (AGS-101) at about $146 to $152, so the default says "about $150". A plain
  Game Boy Advance is cheaper (about $50 to $85 loose), which is why the line
  names the SP. Re-check it now and then.
  The chart compares against a VINTAGE HANDHELD, not "knockoffs": every row is
  true of any original handheld, and nothing is claimed about a competitor
  that cannot be shown.

  WHERE THINGS SIT ON A PHONE. pg-r36s-mobile makes .pgx-buy a flex column under
  900px and gives every child an order (title 1, stars 2, BUNDLE & SAVE 3,
  tiles 4, add to cart 5, sellout 6 to 9, info 10, payment 11, guarantee 12,
  accordions 13). The benefits take 2, so they land right after the stars.
  pg-mobile re-seats the review card after the stars every 1.5s; order, not
  DOM position, is what keeps the benefits above it on a phone.

  THE TRUST MODULES COME STRAIGHT AFTER THE BUNDLES (2026-09-17, by request:
  "move these modules right below the last bundle"). The shipping row, the
  payment icons, the guarantee bar and the Description / Features accordions
  used to sit under the review card AND the photo strip, a long way below the
  button. The review card now takes order 14 and the photo strip 15, so a phone
  reads tiles | add to cart | sellout | info | payment | guarantee | accordions
  | review card | buyer photos. On desktop there is no flex order, so the photo
  strip is seated at the END of the buy column for the same result.
  THE PHOTO STRIP MOVED UP UNDER THE BUNDLES (2026-09-17, by request: "the
  scrollable buyer reviews module should be right under the duo max bundle").
  On a phone it takes order 5, so the run is tiles | buyer reviews | sellout |
  accordions | info | payment | guarantee | review card. On a desktop it is
  seated after the Add to cart button, not between the bundles and the button,
  so the button does not drop 400px down the column.
  THE ACCORDIONS LEAD THAT BLOCK (2026-09-17, by request: "move the description
  features shipping buttons right below the sellout risk module"). On a phone
  they take the sellout slot's order (6) and follow it in the DOM, so the run
  is tiles | sellout | accordions | info | payment | guarantee. On desktop the
  sellout box sits above the Add to cart button, and nothing is put between
  the bundles and that button, so there the accordions come straight after the
  button, ahead of the info box: they are moved in the DOM to just before
  .pgx-info. pg-acc-place only re-seats them when they have left the buy
  column, so the two do not fight.

  YOU MAY ALSO LIKE GOES NEAR THE BOTTOM. pg-theme-css builds that block late
  (after a catalog fetch) and drops it right under the product, which put it
  ahead of this whole story. The script here keeps the lower page in the order
  product | story | you may also like | reviews. It re-checks when the parent's
  children change (that is how the late block is caught) and does nothing once
  the order is right. pg-yml-last does the same job on the other pages but is
  NOT used here: it and this file would both claim the seat before the reviews.

  ONE MODULE, FOUR CHAPTERS. The story began as headings and text on one
  continuous dark ground and read as a single block ("make each section more
  distinct"); it became four separate rounded panels; those were joined into
  one long panel ("make the modules flow more together"), split into cards
  again ("I like the rounded corners and how it was before"), and joined once
  more (2026-09-17: "reconnect all those modules instead of individual
  cards"). What settled it is the glow: the sections are JOINED, the first
  carries the rounded top and the last the rounded bottom, a hairline divides
  them with the purple bar sitting on it, and EVERY section opens with the
  soft purple glow at its top ("at the top add that purple glow so people know
  it's a new section"), fading out on its own.
  The reviews open with a "Customer Reviews" HEADING (a CSS label, scoped to
  this template). It was the small pill the story sections wear, which works
  inside a panel but floated on its own between You may also like and the
  left-aligned 4.6 block ("looks awkward there"): it is a plain centred title
  now, the size of the page's other section titles. The rule that ran across
  the page above it is gone by request ("take out lines"). You may also like had a panel too for a few hours
  and lost it again by request ("doesn't need to be in a module"): it is the
  theme's plain block, heading and cards.

  NOTHING WRAPS BY ACCIDENT ON A PHONE (2026-09-17, by report, with
  screenshots from a 393px iPhone). Inside a panel the text column is about
  313 to 331px, and three things broke badly there: the price cards ("Used,
  one system, no / games", and "CHOOSE YOUR BUNDLE" with its arrow alone on a
  second line), the lead under them (a last line of just "it."), and the
  headline (the purple sentence split "Without a / Single Game.").
    - the price cards say what they say in two fixed lines each, none of which
      can wrap, and the link is "See bundles" (measured: the widest line is
      116px in a 118px column at 360px, the tightest common phone);
    - headlines are balanced and the purple sentence is its own line under
      900px (27px type, 25px under 380px: it fits on one line from 360px up);
    - leads use text-wrap:pretty, and their last two words are tied together
      with a non-breaking space for browsers without it.
  THE ICONS ARE BIGGER (same report, then again: "the 4 icons under title are
  so tiny"). The first answer kept the two-by-two layout and took the icons
  from 32px to 46px, which on the owner's 440px iPhone was still small marks in
  a wide, mostly empty row. They are FOUR ACROSS now, icon above label, the
  way the page this was modelled on shows them: the icon is 84% of its column
  up to 74px (74px at 440px wide, 69px at 393px, 65px at 375px), so it grows
  with the phone instead of stopping at a fixed size. On a phone only the bold
  label shows (two short lines); the second line comes back from 601px up,
  where a column has room for it. Under the hood went from 50px to 64px on a
  phone and 58px to 72px on a desktop; then, by request ("make white icons
  within purple circle bigger"), the white drawing inside went from half the
  circle to about 62% of it (40px in 64px on a phone, 44px in 72px on desktop).
  THE FOUR UNDER THE TITLE MATCH THEM (2026-09-17: "make the icons under the
  title like the ones further down, they're brighter white"). They were a
  translucent purple disc with a lavender ring and a lavender drawing. They are
  the same solid purple gradient disc and pure white drawing as Under the hood.
  A LITTLE SMALLER, WITH BIGGER LABELS (same day: "make the 4 purple circles a
  little smaller, not too much ... maybe adjust font so it's bigger and easier
  to read"). The disc is 74% of its column up to 64px (it was 84% up to 74px)
  and the label is 13.5px on a phone, 14px above that (it was 12.5px); 12.5px
  from 370px down, where a column is about 80px and "Preloaded" has to fit.

  THE NOSTALGIA SECTION HAS A PICTURE. On the Ultra page (2026-09-23) both
  photos are picked by exact alt text, the way pg-r36h-story does it: "Pocket
  Era R36S Ultra in Transparent Purple, angled" (the joystick-glow hero) sits
  in "Your childhood, upgraded", and "Pocket Era R36S Ultra in Transparent
  Purple" (the front shot) goes beside the price comparison. Each falls back
  to the featured image. Both can be replaced in the theme editor.

  THE PRICE CARD IS A BUTTON. The highlighted price card in "Do the math"
  looks like the thing to tap, so it is one: it scrolls up to the bundles, the
  same as the button at the foot of the story.

  SPEC TILES AND THE CHILDHOOD SLOGAN (2026-09-22, by request, rolled out from
  the R36H page). Each Under the hood card now leads with a big stat drawn
  from its own title, over its original description, unchanged. The childhood
  panel closes with "The games you remember. The feeling you forgot."
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product -%}
{%- comment -%} the three accessory cards show the ADD-ON PRODUCTS' own pictures (2026-09-21: the case renders were redone with one unit each; a fixed file name in Files kept showing the old two-case shot, "look this still shows 2"). 2026-09-23, Ultra page: the r36s-ultra-* add-ons, and no Files fallback, because those renders show the Pro's accessories; a card whose add-on has no picture shows its words only {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign uls_sil = all_products['r36s-ultra-silicone-case'] -%}
{%- assign uls_hard = all_products['r36s-ultra-hard-shell-case'] -%}
{%- assign uls_prot = all_products['r36s-ultra-screen-protector'] -%}
{%- assign uls_sil_img = '' -%}{%- if uls_sil.featured_image -%}{%- assign uls_sil_img = uls_sil.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign uls_hard_img = '' -%}{%- if uls_hard.featured_image -%}{%- assign uls_hard_img = uls_hard.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign uls_prot_img = '' -%}{%- if uls_prot.featured_image -%}{%- assign uls_prot_img = uls_prot.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} 2026-09-23, Ultra page: the Judge.me feed is not read here at all (this product's reviews were imported for the Flip SP), and the two photos are picked by exact alt, the way pg-r36h-story does it: the angled purple shot with the joystick glow in "Your childhood, upgraded", the purple front shot beside the price comparison; each falls back to the featured image {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign uls_hero = product.images | where: 'alt', 'Pocket Era R36S Ultra in Transparent Purple, angled' | first -%}
{%- assign hero_img = section.settings.hero_image | default: uls_hero | default: product.featured_image -%}
{%- assign uls_story = product.images | where: 'alt', 'Pocket Era R36S Ultra in Transparent Purple' | first -%}
{%- assign story_img = section.settings.story_image | default: uls_story | default: product.featured_image -%}
<style>
  /* ---------------- 1. benefits ---------------- */
  /* four across, icon over label; the icon scales with its column */
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben{list-style:none !important;margin:6px 0 18px !important;padding:0 !important;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben li{list-style:none !important;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;text-align:center;gap:9px;margin:0 !important;padding:0 !important;min-width:0;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;color:#CFC4DE}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben li:before{content:none !important}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben .ic{flex:none;width:74%;max-width:64px;aspect-ratio:1/1;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    background:rgba(139,68,190,.3);border:0;
    box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(199,155,234,.38),0 0 20px 0 rgba(139,68,190,.45)}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben .ic svg{width:56%;height:56%;stroke:#D9B4FF;fill:none;stroke-width:2;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben li > span:last-child{display:block;min-width:0;max-width:100%}
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben b{display:block;margin-bottom:2px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800;color:#fff;text-wrap:balance}
  /* the number of games: its own line, white like the rest of the label */
  #pgx .pg-uls-ben b i{display:block;font-style:normal;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap}
  /* the stars and review count lead the title (2026-09-17). A phone's buy
     column is a flex column, so the rating takes order 0 ahead of the title's
     1; a desktop's is block, so the rating is lifted to the column's top and
     the title makes room for it (pg-mobile's quoteUp keeps the review card
     after the rating in the DOM, which now sits under the title on screen).
     The title balances its two lines. */
  #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-title{text-wrap:balance}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* the stars hug the photo above and stand off the title (2026-09-18: "too close to title") */
    /* UNDER the title since 2026-09-19 evening, the way the orb page has it (owner: "do the verified reviews thing like 110 verified reviews under the titles for the consoles like the orb has it") */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-rating{order:1;margin:2px 0 14px}
  }
  @media (min-width:901px){
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy{position:relative}
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-rating{position:static;margin:4px 0 14px}
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-title{padding-top:0}
  }

  /* ---------------- 2. buyer photos ---------------- */
  /* removed on the Ultra page (2026-09-23) with the strip itself: this
     product's Judge.me reviews were imported for the Flip SP */

  /* ---------------- 3. the story ---------------- */
  .pg-uls{font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#F1EDF7;background:#0B0710}
  /* inside #pgx the page's own dark gradient shows through; the solid fill is
     only for the moment before the script seats it there */
  #pgx .pg-uls{background:transparent}
  .pg-uls *{box-sizing:border-box}
  #pgx .pg-uls{padding:26px 0 6px}
  /* one module, four chapters: the sections are joined, the first carries the
     rounded top and the last the rounded bottom, a hairline divides them, and
     every one opens with the purple glow at its top */
  .pg-uls-sec{position:relative;width:calc(100% - 48px);max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:58px 44px 54px;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;
    border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.22);border-bottom-width:0;border-radius:0;
    background:radial-gradient(90% 62% at 50% 0%,rgba(155,75,196,.22),rgba(155,75,196,0) 72%),rgba(255,255,255,.03)}
  .pg-uls-sec + .pg-uls-sec{border-top-color:rgba(199,155,234,.14)}
  .pg-uls-sec:first-child{border-radius:28px 28px 0 0}
  .pg-uls-sec:last-child{border-bottom-width:1px;border-radius:0 0 28px 28px;margin-bottom:28px;box-shadow:0 34px 80px -60px rgba(139,68,190,.95)}
  .pg-uls-sec:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:50%;top:0;width:96px;height:3px;margin-left:-48px;border-radius:0 0 4px 4px;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,#9B4BC4,#D9B3F5)}
  .pg-uls-eye{display:inline-block;margin:0 0 16px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;
    border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.42);background:rgba(155,75,196,.16);
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C79BEA}
  /* the reviews open with a real title, centred, and no rule across the page */
  #pgx #pg-reviews{border-top:0;margin-top:8px;padding-top:34px}
  #pgx #pg-reviews:before{content:"Customer Reviews";display:block;margin:0 0 28px;text-align:center;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:32px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}
  .pg-uls h2{margin:0 auto 14px;max-width:820px;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:40px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff;text-wrap:balance}
  .pg-uls h2 span{background:linear-gradient(100deg,#F3E8FF 0%,#D9B3F5 30%,#B06CE8 60%,#8B3FB8 100%);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent}
  .pg-uls-lead{margin:0 auto;max-width:640px;font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#CFC4DE;text-wrap:pretty}
  .pg-uls-lead b{color:#fff}
  /* the closing line of the childhood panel (2026-09-22, by request, the same on every console page) */
  .pg-uls-mem{margin:18px 0 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:3px solid #9B4BC4;font-size:17px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;color:#D9B3F5}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    .pg-uls-mem{margin:16px auto 0;padding:0;border:0;font-size:15.5px;text-align:center}
  }

  .pg-uls-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:44px;align-items:center;text-align:left}
  .pg-uls-split h2,.pg-uls-split .pg-uls-lead{margin-left:0;margin-right:0}
  .pg-uls-photo{border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);background:#16101F;box-shadow:0 30px 70px -40px rgba(139,68,190,.8)}
  .pg-uls-photo img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/1;object-fit:cover}
  /* 2026-09-23, Ultra page: the photo beside the price comparison is the purple front shot, so its crop is centred (the Pro's gloves shot favoured its lower half) */
  .pg-uls-sec:not(.pg-uls-hero) .pg-uls-photo img{object-position:50% 50%}
  .pg-uls-hero .pg-uls-photo{order:-1}
  .pg-uls-math{display:flex;gap:12px;margin:22px 0 0}
  .pg-uls-math div{flex:1;min-width:0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:14px;background:#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09)}
  .pg-uls-math small,.pg-uls-math em,.pg-uls-math .go{white-space:nowrap}
  .pg-uls-math div.us{border-color:rgba(199,155,234,.55);background:linear-gradient(140deg,#1D1230,#16101F);cursor:pointer;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;transition:transform .15s ease,border-color .15s ease,box-shadow .15s ease}
  .pg-uls-math div.us:hover,.pg-uls-math div.us:focus-visible{border-color:#C79BEA;box-shadow:0 14px 30px -18px rgba(155,75,196,.95);transform:translateY(-2px);outline:0}
  .pg-uls-math div.us:active{transform:translateY(0)}
  .pg-uls-math .go{display:block;margin-top:9px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C79BEA}
  /* the top bar is pinned, so a jump to the bundles stops short of it */
  #pgx .pgx-bs{scroll-margin-top:76px}
  .pg-uls-math small{display:block;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B9AECB}
  .pg-uls-math strong{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:26px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1.1}
  .pg-uls-math em{display:block;margin-top:3px;font-style:normal;font-size:12.5px;color:#CFC4DE}

  .pg-uls-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:18px;margin:34px 0 0}
  /* spec tiles (2026-09-22, by request): a big stat drawn from each card's title over its original description */
  .pg-uls-feat{position:relative;padding:32px 18px 30px;border-radius:22px;overflow:hidden;
    background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(155,75,196,.14),rgba(155,75,196,0) 60%),#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.18)}
  .pg-uls-feat .ic{width:72px;height:72px;margin:0 auto 16px;border-radius:20px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    background:linear-gradient(135deg,#C48EEA 0%,#A85DD3 35%,#8F3FB8 65%,#5A2280 100%);box-shadow:0 12px 26px -14px rgba(155,75,196,.9)}
  .pg-uls-feat .ic svg{width:54px;height:54px;stroke:#fff;fill:none;stroke-width:1.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
  /* the stat words carry a slow white-to-lavender sweep (2026-09-22, "should be moving"); the gradient repeats every element width, so a 200% travel loops without a jump */
  .pg-uls-feat h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-family:inherit;font-size:26px;line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;text-wrap:balance;
    background:linear-gradient(100deg,#fff 0%,#D9B3F5 25%,#fff 50%,#D9B3F5 75%,#fff 100%);background-size:200% 100%;background-position:0% 50%;
    -webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;
    animation:pg-uls-statflow 4s linear infinite}
  @keyframes pg-uls-statflow{from{background-position:0% 50%}to{background-position:200% 50%}}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.pg-uls-feat h3{animation:none}}
  /* every description is cut to the same length, so the four cards read as one row (2026-09-22, "all paragraphs need to be the same size") */
  .pg-uls-feat p{margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#CFC4DE;text-wrap:balance}

  /* the accessories chapter (2026-09-19, asked for after the Flip SP's cases
     module: "copy that module for the hard shell and daily case ... for the
     r36s pro one too, but with that one they have to upgrade to max to get
     it, there are no add-ons"): four cards, photo left, name / one line
     right, an "Included" tag on each, a chapter of the same joined module
     between Under the hood and Side by side. The photos are Gemini renders
     in the store's purple studio style (Files: pe-r36pro2-*.jpg, not used on
     the Ultra page). The joystick
     caps card was removed 2026-09-19 ("no joystick caps anywhere"). */
  .pg-uls-cases{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:16px;max-width:1000px;margin:30px auto 0;text-align:left}
  /* three cards since 2026-09-19 ("no joystick caps anywhere"): three across on a desktop, a column on phones */
  .pg-uls-case{grid-template-columns:104px minmax(0,1fr);gap:13px;padding:14px}
  .pg-uls-case img{width:104px;height:104px}
  .pg-uls-case{display:grid;grid-template-columns:124px minmax(0,1fr);gap:16px;align-items:center;padding:16px;border-radius:18px;background:#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09)}
  .pg-uls-case img{display:block;width:124px;height:124px;border-radius:14px;object-fit:cover;background:#0D0714}
  .pg-uls-case .tag{display:inline-block;margin:0 0 7px;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(155,75,196,.2);border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.4);font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C79BEA}
  .pg-uls-case h3{margin:0 0 5px;font-family:inherit;font-size:16px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:800;color:#fff}
  .pg-uls-case p{margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#CFC4DE}
  /* an add-on without a picture (2026-09-23, Ultra page: no Files fallback) shows its words across the card */
  .pg-uls-case.noimg{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}
  .pg-uls-tbl{max-width:720px;margin:34px auto 0;text-align:left}
  .pg-uls-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);align-items:stretch}
  .pg-uls-row > div{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:14px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);font-size:14px;line-height:1.3}
  .pg-uls-row > div:first-child{justify-content:flex-start;padding-left:4px;font-weight:600;color:#F1EDF7}
  .pg-uls-row > div.us{background:#1A1129;border-left:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.45);border-right:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.45)}
  .pg-uls-row.hd > div{border-bottom:0;padding:16px 8px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:800;text-align:center;color:#fff}
  .pg-uls-row.hd > div.us{border-top:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.45);border-radius:16px 16px 0 0}
  .pg-uls-row.hd > div.them{color:#B9AECB;font-weight:700}
  .pg-uls-row:last-child > div{border-bottom:0}
  .pg-uls-row:last-child > div.us{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.45);border-radius:0 0 16px 16px}
  .pg-uls-tbl .y,.pg-uls-tbl .n{width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex:none}
  .pg-uls-tbl .y{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2)}
  .pg-uls-tbl .n{background:#2A2236}
  .pg-uls-tbl .y svg,.pg-uls-tbl .n svg{width:13px;height:13px;fill:none;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:2.6;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
  .pg-uls-tbl .n svg{stroke:#8E829F}

  .pg-uls-cta{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:9px;margin:36px 0 0;padding:16px 34px;border-radius:12px;cursor:pointer;
    background-color:#7A2FA2;background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 30%,#4A1C66 50%,#7A2FA2 70%,#9B4BC4 100%);background-size:240% 240%;
    color:#fff !important;font-size:15px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none !important;
    box-shadow:0 16px 34px -14px rgba(139,68,190,.8);-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none}
  .pg-uls-cta:hover{filter:brightness(1.08)}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-uls-ben{order:2}
    /* a little air between the white guarantee bar and the review card under
       it. It goes on the BAR: pg-mobile stamps margin:0 0 16px !important
       inline on the review card every 1.5s, so the card's own top margin
       cannot be set from a stylesheet. */
    /* 2026-09-18, "move the 30 day money back guarantee module above the picture
       carousel": the guarantee bar joins the order-5 run after the payment icons,
       so the photo strip (6) follows it */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-guar{order:5;margin-bottom:18px !important}
    /* the accordions follow the sellout slot (order 6, earlier in the DOM) */
    /* 2026-09-18: the accordions sit right under the sellout card, ahead of the trust row */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-acc{order:5;margin-top:0 !important}
    /* two ids: pg-r36s-mobile gives the review card order 8 at one */
    /* the rotating review card sits right under the bundles, ahead of the
       sellout card (2026-09-18: above the bundles it pushed Add to cart down,
       "add to cart gets too low"). Order 5, and it leads that run because it
       comes first in the DOM. */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-quote{order:5}
    /* the photo strip: straight after the tiles (4), ahead of the sellout
       slot and the accordions (6) */
    /* 2026-09-17, "put the sellout risk module above the buyer review photos":
       the sellout card takes order 5 too and precedes the strip in the DOM, so
       it lands first; the strip then closes the block above the accordions */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-sell-slot{order:5;margin-top:0 !important;margin-bottom:8px !important}
    /* 2026-09-18, "the ships by, easy returns and credit card icons need to be
       moved up": the trust row and the payment icons follow the sellout card,
       ahead of the photo strip; the strip (6, before the accordions in the DOM)
       then leads the accordions */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-info{order:5;margin-top:14px}
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-pay{order:5}
    #pgx .pg-uls{padding-top:18px}
    .pg-uls-sec{width:calc(100% - 24px);padding:36px 18px 32px}
    .pg-uls-sec:first-child{border-radius:22px 22px 0 0}
    .pg-uls-sec:last-child{border-radius:0 0 22px 22px;margin-bottom:16px}
    #pgx #pg-reviews{margin-top:4px;padding-top:28px}
    #pgx #pg-reviews:before{font-size:26px;margin-bottom:22px}
    /* on a phone the words come first and the picture closes the panel */
    .pg-uls-hero .pg-uls-photo{order:0}
    .pg-uls-hero .pg-uls-photo img{aspect-ratio:4/5}
    .pg-uls h2{font-size:27px;line-height:1.15}
    /* the purple sentence starts its own line, and fits on one */
    .pg-uls h2 span{display:block}
    .pg-uls-lead{font-size:15px}
    .pg-uls-split{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px;text-align:center}
    .pg-uls-split h2,.pg-uls-split .pg-uls-lead{margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}
    .pg-uls-math{text-align:left;gap:10px}
    .pg-uls-math div{padding:14px 12px}
    .pg-uls-math small{font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em}
    .pg-uls-math em{font-size:12px}
    .pg-uls-math .go{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.06em}
    .pg-uls-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:26px}
    .pg-uls-feat{padding:24px 8px 22px;border-radius:20px}
    .pg-uls-feat .ic{width:60px;height:60px;margin-bottom:12px;border-radius:17px}
    .pg-uls-feat .ic svg{width:46px;height:46px}
    .pg-uls-feat h3{font-size:clamp(20px,5.8vw,24px);margin-bottom:6px}
    .pg-uls-feat p{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45}
    .pg-uls-cases{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:22px}
    .pg-uls-case{grid-template-columns:96px minmax(0,1fr);gap:13px;padding:13px}
    .pg-uls-case img{width:96px;height:96px}
    .pg-uls-case h3{font-size:15px}
    .pg-uls-case p{font-size:12.5px}
    .pg-uls-tbl{margin-top:26px}
    .pg-uls-row > div{font-size:13px;padding:12px 6px}
    .pg-uls-row.hd > div{font-size:12.5px;padding:13px 6px}
    .pg-uls-cta{display:flex;width:100%;margin-top:28px;padding:16px 12px}
  }
  /* phones: the bold label only, in two short lines under a big icon. The
     second line is a bare text node, so it is hidden by zeroing the span's
     type and giving the label its size back. */
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben{gap:6px}
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben li{gap:8px}
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben li > span:last-child{font-size:0;line-height:0}
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben b{margin:0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.22}
  }
  @media (max-width:370px){
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben b{font-size:10.5px}
  }
  @media (max-width:380px){
    .pg-uls h2{font-size:25px}
    .pg-uls-math strong{font-size:22px}
  }
  /* the very narrow phones */
  @media (max-width:340px){
    #pgx .pg-uls-ben b{font-size:10px}
    .pg-uls-math small{font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.03em}
    .pg-uls-math em{font-size:11px}
  }
</style>

